course: dictionary
lesson: 15560
title: Supposition: a guess with reasons
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A supposition is an idea you think is true but have not proved yet. It is a guess, but a sensible one, because you have some reasons for it. «Her idea that the cat ate the cake was pure supposition, because nobody had seen it.»
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «The detective said, "That is just supposition. Show me some proof."» The detective is saying the idea has no proof yet, so it is not a fact. Ask yourself: has this been proved, or is it still a guess?
explain: Supposition is also a word for the act of guessing rather than knowing. «On the supposition that the bus is late, we will walk.» We do not know the bus is late. We are planning as if it might be, and that is what supposing means.
fact: A supposition is an idea or belief that you think is true but have not proved.
fact: «Supposition» means a guess based on some reasons, not on certain knowledge.
fact: Useful phrases: «pure supposition», «on the supposition that», «based on supposition».
fact: In science, a supposition is like a hypothesis, and it needs testing before we can be sure.
fact: In maths, you can make a supposition, such as «Suppose x is 5», and then work out what follows.
exercise: Tom says the thief was his brother, but he has no proof. His idea is «pure supposition». What is a supposition? | A loud shout of surprise | *An idea you think is true but have not proved | A type of sweet | A fact that a scientist has checked
exercise: The detective said, «That's just supposition. Find me some proof.» What does the detective mean? | *There is no proof yet | The suspect is innocent | The case is closed | The answer is definitely correct
exercise: «We will set off on the supposition that the bus is late.» Find the word that means a guess based on reasons. | bus | late | *supposition | set
test: «Based on supposition, the scientist wrote a hypothesis and planned a test.» In science, what must be done with a supposition? | Believe it without testing | Forget it because it is a fact | *Test it to see if it is true | Make it into a song
test: Mia says, «I suppose the shop is open, but I have not checked.» What is Mia's idea? | A checked fact | *A guess that is not yet proved | A rule of maths | A famous quote
exam: In maths you write «Suppose x is 5». What does this ask you to do? | Skip the question | *Assume x is 5 and work out what follows | Find a new value for x by guessing | Prove that x is not 5
